  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946716/assets/0896ba394361067fd7cfcb57d194d25218a30d64974caf99c0458a6cf27c35d5.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            The function $f$ is part of the exponential curve $y={5}^{x-a}+b$ shown in the figure above. Find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $a\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n\n$\\,b\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the horizontal asymptote of $y={5}^{x-a}+b$ is $y=b.$ \n\nIn the figure above, the horizontal asymptote is $y=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Hence, $b=\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nNext, we use the point $(3,\\frac{5}{2})$ to determine the value of $a.$\nSubstituting $(3,\\frac{5}{2})$ into the equation of the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{3-a}+\\frac{3}{2} & =\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ {5}^{3-a} & =1 \\\\ 3-a & =0 \\\\ a & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3$ and $b=\\frac{3}{2}.$",
